// TEST: an Int64 row's sum plus 0.5 in a generic body is refused at the call (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019
// ============================================================================
// `reduce(row, (+))` over a `row: T^1` is a scalar of the row's element; at
// an Int64 row, `+ 0.5` would convert it implicitly. The body that means
// Float64 arithmetic converts first: `Float64(reduce(row, (+))) + 0.5`.
// ============================================================================
function f(row: T^1) = reduce(row, (+)) + 0.5
let v = f([1, 2])
